  <p style=3D"margin:0 0 12px 0;font-family:'Segoe UI',Tahoma,Geneva,Verdana,=
sans-serif;font-size:15px;color:#555555;line-height:1.7;">
    Last issue, we named the Holographic Memory pattern. This issue, we build=
 it &mdash; step by step in Copilot Studio.</p>
  <p style=3D"margin:0 0 12px 0;font-family:'Segoe UI',Tahoma,Geneva,Verdana,=
sans-serif;font-size:15px;color:#555555;line-height:1.7;">
    Your customer just asked: "Can we build one agent that answers questions =
across all our projects &#8212; even when those projects share nothing in com=
mon?" They have design docs in SharePoint, decision records in repos, and mee=
ting notes from <a href=3D"https://microsoft.github.io/ai-cheatcode/issues/th=
e_cheat_code_issue_006.html" style=3D"color:#6B2FA0;text-decoration:underline=
;">Issue #006</a>'s pipeline. Each data source is a silo. No single agent con=
nects them today.
  </p>
  <p style=3D"margin:0;font-family:'Segoe UI',Tahoma,Geneva,Verdana,sans-seri=
f;font-size:15px;color:#555555;line-height:1.7;">
    <strong>This issue's pattern:</strong> A cross-project knowledge agent bu=
ilt in Copilot Studio that uses enriched Azure AI Search to synthesize answer=
s across project boundaries &#8212; even when the source documents never refe=
rence each other.
  </p>
</td></tr>

<!-- AGENT SPOTLIGHT -->
